WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.393
- Good morning Believe Nation!

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:02.819
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.819 --> 00:00:05.721
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.721 --> 00:00:09.220
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.508
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.508 --> 00:00:11.983
today we're going to learn about

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:15.071
how to not worry about
what other people say.

00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:17.021
Over to you, Brett Favre.

00:00:17.021 --> 00:00:19.135
(rooster crowing)

00:00:19.135 --> 00:00:21.669
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.669 --> 00:00:24.420
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.422
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.422 --> 00:00:31.252
- You know, for me, my
career has been awesome.

00:00:31.252 --> 00:00:32.969
There's probably decisions I wish

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:34.327
I would have made differently

00:00:34.327 --> 00:00:36.791
and as I look to the future

00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:38.765
there'll probably be the same thing.

00:00:38.765 --> 00:00:41.224
You know? In all phases of life.

00:00:41.224 --> 00:00:45.391
And I don't worry about what
people say, good or bad.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:49.453
We would all love good
things to be said about us.

00:00:49.453 --> 00:00:51.487
It sure is nice to pick up
the paper, turn on the news,

00:00:51.487 --> 00:00:54.128
and good things are said about you.

00:00:54.128 --> 00:00:55.443
And that's not always the case.

00:00:55.443 --> 00:00:57.821
So I don't really pay attention to it.

00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:01.564
I really feel like my
character speaks for itself.

00:01:01.564 --> 00:01:04.419
The way I've played the game,
the way I've carried myself

00:01:04.419 --> 00:01:06.594
It's not always been perfect.

00:01:06.594 --> 00:01:11.240
But I'm very proud of what
I've done on and off the field.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.301
And, ultimately, that is
the most important thing,

00:01:15.301 --> 00:01:17.154
is how we feel about ourselves.

00:01:17.154 --> 00:01:18.822
- It's important to
understand that the minute

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:20.873
that you start to do something different,

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.781
the minute that you
start to try to stand up

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:24.520
from the crowd and go do your own thing,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.350
that's the minute that you start

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.632
to get criticized by other people.

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:32.246
If you don't do the thing that
your family wants you to do,

00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:35.020
if you don't do the thing that
your friends want you to do,

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.629
or your culture wants you to do,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.854
as soon as you start to lay your own path

00:01:39.854 --> 00:01:42.169
and say, "This is the
direction that I want to go in

00:01:42.169 --> 00:01:43.615
and be different,"

00:01:43.615 --> 00:01:46.551
that's when you start to open
yourself up to criticism.

00:01:46.551 --> 00:01:48.849
Cause people are one, afraid

00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:51.104
that you're off doing this
thing that's different

00:01:51.104 --> 00:01:53.918
and it's not normal and it's unsafe

00:01:53.918 --> 00:01:56.283
and so we're going to
tear down that person.

00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:57.912
People are going to be jealous of you,

00:01:57.912 --> 00:02:01.160
saying "I wish I could go and
do that, but I'm too afraid

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.968
to go do that myself, so I'm
just going to stay in my corner

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.335
and just throw tomatoes at that person."

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:08.433
People, also out of
love, will criticize you.

00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:11.241
Because they thing that your
path should be the normal,

00:02:11.241 --> 00:02:13.968
safe one instead of going off
and doing that scary thing.

00:02:13.968 --> 00:02:16.016
So as entrepreneurs that's something

00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:16.928
we all will come up against.

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:19.600
Because by the very nature of what we do,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.733
we're off doing different things.

00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:23.444
We're off trying to create a new world.

00:02:23.444 --> 00:02:25.425
We're off trying to invent
something different.

00:02:25.425 --> 00:02:27.152
We want to change the way things are done.

00:02:27.152 --> 00:02:30.631
And whenever you stand out
you're going to get criticism.

00:02:30.631 --> 00:02:33.166
And so, at the start I think it's

00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:35.563
one, understanding that, recognizing that,

00:02:35.563 --> 00:02:37.373
trying to put yourself
in that person's shoes

00:02:37.373 --> 00:02:39.871
and say, "Listen, this
person who's criticizing me

00:02:39.871 --> 00:02:42.391
just doesn't get it," instead
of taking it personally.

00:02:42.391 --> 00:02:44.572
Because what happens to a lot of people,

00:02:44.572 --> 00:02:46.743
when they get that criticism,

00:02:46.743 --> 00:02:48.406
is they shut down.

00:02:48.406 --> 00:02:49.401
They can't handle it.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:50.778
They're not used to it.

00:02:50.778 --> 00:02:52.045
So they shrink.

00:02:52.045 --> 00:02:53.619
So they have this bold goal,

00:02:53.619 --> 00:02:55.831
this bold mission of
where they want to go,

00:02:55.831 --> 00:02:57.672
and then as soon as somebody attacks them,

00:02:57.672 --> 00:03:00.238
the yshrink back down and think,
"Maybe I shouldn't do that.

00:03:00.238 --> 00:03:01.990
Maybe I shouldn't go for that."

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.806
And so you cancel your
own dream because of

00:03:03.806 --> 00:03:06.525
other people expectations on you.

00:03:06.525 --> 00:03:09.820
I remember when I made
my first Believe video.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.032
I showed it to somebody who I respected

00:03:12.032 --> 00:03:13.469
in the film industry

00:03:13.469 --> 00:03:14.736
and he didn't like it.

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:15.732
He said it was too long

00:03:15.732 --> 00:03:17.559
and nobody would ever watch it

00:03:17.559 --> 00:03:19.078
and that I should cut it down.

00:03:19.078 --> 00:03:20.534
And he told me that I
didn't understand how

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:21.839
the internet worked.

00:03:21.839 --> 00:03:23.875
And I looked at the video again,

00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:25.612
and this was a guy who
understood the industry,

00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:28.482
not some outsider who doesn't
really understand anything,

00:03:28.482 --> 00:03:30.860
just people throwing
their opinions at you,

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.004
he understood the industry

00:03:32.004 --> 00:03:32.918
and I looked at the video again

00:03:32.918 --> 00:03:34.398
and, you know what, I just loved it.

00:03:34.398 --> 00:03:35.819
I loved the video

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:37.922
and even if it was a complete flop,

00:03:37.922 --> 00:03:42.097
I still had to put it out,
because it meant something to me.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.426
Now, luckily, the video did well.

00:03:44.426 --> 00:03:46.551
The video had 100,000
views in the first month,

00:03:46.551 --> 00:03:48.313
it's sitting at over 2,000,000 views now.

00:03:48.313 --> 00:03:50.755
The video became the best video

00:03:50.755 --> 00:03:53.279
that I had on my channel at the time.

00:03:53.279 --> 00:03:55.146
But not everything is going to work out.

00:03:55.146 --> 00:03:56.743
Some thing are going to fail.

00:03:56.743 --> 00:03:58.625
Some things you're going to flop on.

00:03:58.625 --> 00:03:59.656
You're not going to have great results

00:03:59.656 --> 00:04:00.489
at the beginning of anything,

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:02.995
because you're learning a new skill.

00:04:02.995 --> 00:04:04.970
What's important to understand is,

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.597
you need to make a decision
at some point in your life,

00:04:07.597 --> 00:04:10.321
that you're going to live
your version of your life

00:04:10.321 --> 00:04:12.595
instead of somebody else's
version of your life,

00:04:12.595 --> 00:04:16.173
because everybody else has a
plan for what you should do

00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:19.501
and until you decide to break free

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.092
and run with your own plan

00:04:21.092 --> 00:04:24.564
and deal with the criticism
that will come alongside it

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.389
then you're never going
to go off and accomplish

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:28.626
the big things that you have in your head.

00:04:28.626 --> 00:04:31.357
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:04:31.357 --> 00:04:34.465
what was some harsh feedback that you got

00:04:34.465 --> 00:04:37.440
on your business idea,
or in your personal life,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.883
that hurt you for a while.

00:04:39.883 --> 00:04:42.547
And maybe by spreading it
here, you can release it.

00:04:42.547 --> 00:04:44.096
Release it from your system so that

00:04:44.096 --> 00:04:46.077
it no longer bothers you.

00:04:46.077 --> 00:04:47.171
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:04:47.171 --> 00:04:48.963
I'm really curious to find out.

00:04:48.963 --> 00:04:49.796
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Alfred Gonzalez,

00:04:49.796 --> 00:04:52.620
Alfred, that you so much for picking up

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.642
a copy of my book. You're One Word,

